<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11559"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 9:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Which airport? The one in Utah is Saltlake City The one in Wichita is Probably ITC, The plane was non-comercial transport so it was a private plane, and Piper doesn&#39;t make huge planes, so it could have landed almost any of the airfields in Wichita, but the report says Wichita so I would say ITC. The part that says Airport-Piper refers to airplaine registration...Piper airport is in Pennsylvania where Piper is headquartered.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11559-->
<!--Post: 11560--><!--Time: 1110907893-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11560"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 9:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Embersage - I tried to look up the coordinates but came up short.  The NTSB report only lists the incident airport as &#39;Piper&#39;.  Of the 8 airports currently listed in the Wichita area, none are named Piper. <BR> <BR>I also checked a website devoted to abandonded and little known airfields and there are none listed at all for Wichita, let alone one named Piper.  Same for the rest of the state of KS. <BR> <BR>The plane involved in the crash was a Piper, so it seems odd that the name of the field was Piper as well.  Yes, most airplane manufacturers have their own fields &#40;there is a Cessna and Beechcraft field in Wichita&#41; but I believe Pipers were manufactured in Florida and before that Pennsylvania.  Perhaps they had a Wichita operation as well.  And I suppose there is no requirement that a field named &#39;Piper&#39; be associated with the manufacturer of the same name, so who knows?..... <BR> <BR>Perhaps a local/native might have more information about the coordinates or know of a &#39;Piper&#39; field in Wichita. <BR> <BR>Just out of curiosity, what is your interest in the coordinates? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11560-->
<!--Post: 11574--><!--Time: 1110917275-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11574"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 12:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Roughly Quoted From The Wichita Beacon <BR> <BR> <BR>In the early stages of the investigation, the possibility that the murders may have been drug-related   <BR>was examined. The Oteros were newly arrived from Puerto Rico and Otero had taken a job as an   <BR>aircraft mechanic at Cook Air Field in Rose Hill. The possible connection came when a plane crashed   <BR>in Miami the day before the murders. The plane was believed to be en route to Wichita from Puerto   <BR>Rico and carried 1 1/2 tons of marijuana.  <BR>   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11574-->
<!--Post: 11593--><!--Time: 1110929545-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11593"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 3:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule - thanks for that information.  However, I don&#39;t think this is the same plane crash.  The crash Embersage is inquiring about originated in Salt Lake City &#40;last I checked not the drug distribution hub of the world&#41; and the crash itself was in Wichita when the plane attempted to land. <BR> <BR>Embersage - can you fill us in on your interest with the crash you referenced in the first post.  Or is the crash Bmodule references the one you are trying to get more information on?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11593-->
<!--Post: 11598--><!--Time: 1110932848-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11598"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 4:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Back when the whole thing started about JOe Otero may have known something and was scared someone mentioned drugs, on the symbol thread we have talked about Paul Raders writing some of his stories were about wild parties and drugs. I never thought much about it until I heard about the plane crash and the drugs. Then while I was reading the messages to BTK thread I realized That BTK was giving us info about someone else, he was writing as if he were writing about BTK but he was not, he was writing about someone else, Makes sense since everything else in his life he took from someone else, In the btk message thread the name Lewis comes up and Utah I knew once I recieved the plane crash information that this is was they were talking about. This is the crash around the same time that Joe was killed I just wondered if one had something to do with the other. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
